# Append-only records. Nine agents in nine worktrees append to these at once, and a
# union merge is the correct resolution: every line is someone's entry and none
# supersedes another. Ordering within the file is not load bearing.
docs/handoffs/current.md   merge=union
exchange/ledger.md         merge=union

# Byte-exact evidence. _recovered/ is the production API as deployed, and a deploy
# from a copy of it is verified by SHA-1 against Vercel's file ids, so git must
# store and check out every byte as it is. Two production files use CRLF
# (api/classify.js, whose prompt text reaches the model, and vercel.json);
# normalising them would change what a redeploy sends. The hotfix beside it is
# deployed from the same copy and gets the same treatment.
_recovered/**                                      -text
council/security/hotfix-2026-09-21-api-comments/** -text
